// Signing for the Mac app: the iPad's team and bundle identifier, with
// entitlements of its own. Apple's browser entitlement is the iPad's; a Mac
// app is a browser by saying it opens web addresses (Mac/Info.plist). It is
// a DMG signed with Developer ID, outside the App Sandbox, with the
// hardened runtime (Config/eGluMac.entitlements says why). Apple's passkey
// entitlement for browsers is in Config/eGluMacReleasePasskeys.entitlements
// alone, for Release/mac.sh with PASSKEYS=1 once Apple has granted it.
//
// iCloud and pushes need a provisioning profile. To run a build signed only
// for this Mac, without them, set in Config/Local.xcconfig (or on
// xcodebuild's command line):
//
//     MAC_ENTITLEMENTS = Config/eGluMacLocal.entitlements
MAC_ENTITLEMENTS = Config/eGluMac.entitlements
// The provisioning profile, for the app alone: Release/mac.sh names the
// Developer ID one (ICLOUD=1) here, since a profile given to every target
// on the command line reaches PadCore's resource bundle too, which can't
// take one. Empty, signing chooses as it would.
MAC_PROFILE =

#include "Signing.xcconfig"

CODE_SIGN_ENTITLEMENTS = $(MAC_ENTITLEMENTS)
PROVISIONING_PROFILE_SPECIFIER = $(MAC_PROFILE)
